# Decode a record
Open the record and decode it to recover its value.

~~~rust
use codec::open;
use codec::decode;
let value = decode(open());
~~~

Reviewed import paths and their exports (other paths were not inspected):
codec: open, wire
codec::wire: decode

Rust use lookup:
To reproduce this use declaration against the reviewed modules, the caller must change the import for decode from codec to codec::wire. Documented: `use codec::decode;`. Available: `use codec::wire::decode;`.
Rust resolves every named use import before compiling the example, including imports of structs and traits. Availability is scoped to the supplied rustdoc build.
open from codec: exported here
decode from codec: absent here; exported by codec::wire
